make measurement errors in a properly

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:59.100
formulated product they will re-measure
the alcohol concentration at the end to

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:02.969
make sure whatever you put in is what
you actually get out pharmaceutical and

00:02:02.969 --> 00:02:06.479
cosmetic grade ingredients are generally
safe to repeatedly put on your hands

00:02:06.479 --> 00:02:10.709
food grade is also generally safe
anything else is a bit of a crapshoot

00:02:10.709 --> 00:02:14.730
the only recipes that I endorse are
the ones that the World Health

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:18.420
Organization has put out and even then
