00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:26.610
sanitizer when you're making a recipe
that has other ingredients apart from

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:30.209
what the World Health Organization has
recommended you are running into a bunch

00:02:30.209 --> 00:02:35.820
of risks these ingredients are water
alcohol glycerin or glycerol and

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:40.380
hydrogen peroxide a lot of people have
asked me if they can add oils to their

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:44.580
hand sanitizers so if you're using
something oil-based essential oils or

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:49.680
vitamin E oil these oils do not mix with
water in a properly formulated product

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:53.670
you have to add solubilisers to make
sure the oil actually disperses and

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:57.840
doesn't just sit on top and so it's
possible you'll squirt out a handful

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:01.920
that is mostly oil and only a tiny bit
