00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:14.100
protect your hands from drying out the
World Health Organization recipes use

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:17.970
glycerin as the moisturizer if you use
other moisturizing ingredients you can

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:22.530
run into problems so for example aloe
vera gel is biological matter that can

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:26.640
go off inside your hand sanitiser aloe
vera gel products do often contain

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:31.380
preservatives but once it's mixed into a
hand sanitizer it might not be preserved

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:35.040
enough even with a really high alcohol
content there's also been a lot of

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:38.760
people saying that aloe vera gel balled
up inside their recipe and they don't

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:42.600
know what to do even if you don't see a
large amount balled up in your recipe

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:46.709
you can have small amounts balled up
that you don't quite notice and so if

00:03:46.709 --> 00:03:50.850
you get a lump of aloe vera gel again
you're going to be dispensing something

00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:54.269
that is less than the required amount of
alcohol onto your hand even if the

00:03:54.269 --> 00:03:58.260
overall product has enough alcohol if
you've added some random moisturizer

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:02.940
into your hand sanitizer you might have
any combination of these problems and I

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:07.019
