what is the difference between ethyl

00:05:56.520 --> 00:06:01.290
alcohol and isopropyl alcohol they are
different ingredients ethanol or ethyl

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:07.500
alcohol has two carbons isopropanol or
isopropyl alcohol has three they are

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:12.480
very similar but they don't have exactly
the same properties ethanol is gentler on

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:16.680
skin than isopropanol in lots of studies
it has been found to be less irritating

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:21.270
isopropyl alcohol is bigger and so you
generally need a slightly higher amount

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:24.210
to have the same effect so it's
recommended that how much ethanol you

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:28.950
put in is somewhere above 60 to 70
percent isopropyl alcohol is above 70

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:32.850
percent what do you do if your source of
alcohol has just high enough concentration

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:36.720
to work I recommend using it as the
sanitizer and then moisturizing your

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:40.890
hands afterwards just remember to make
sure that you let the sanitizer stay in

00:06:40.890 --> 00:06:45.990
contact with your skin for 20 seconds
before you moisturize what do you do if

00:06:45.990 --> 00:06:49.590
your alcohol is lower than 60%
concentration there isn't really much

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:52.500
you can do you can't mix it with
anything to make it a higher

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:56.340
concentration theoretically you could
distill it but I don't recommend doing

00:06:56.340 --> 00:07:00.450
